281-/**
282- * Tiny connection pool reserved for SESSION-level advisory locks
283- * (`sql.reserve()` + `pg_advisory_lock` held across a critical section).
284- *
285- * Holding a session lock requires camping on a physical connection for the
286- * whole critical section. Doing that on the MAIN pool starves it: with
287- * N >= DB_POOL_MAX concurrent holders (or blocked waiters), lock connections
288- * consume every slot and the critical sections' own queries/transactions —
289- * which run on the main pool — can never be served. That is a permanent,
290- * pool-wide deadlock (session advisory waits never time out).
291- *
--
300- * every slot counts against the Postgres connection budget (see the
301- * DB_POOL_MAX note in ci.yml).
